#### question 1
# 1. Let us say your expense for every month are listed below,
# 	1. January -  2200
#  	2. February - 2350
#     3. March - 2600
#     4. April - 2130
#     5. May - 2190
#
# Create a list to store these monthly expenses and using that find out,
#
# 1. In Feb, how many dollars you spent extra compare to January?
# 2. Find out your total expense in first quarter (first three months) of the year.
# 3. Find out if you spent exactly 2000 dollars in any month
# 4. June month just finished and your expense is 1980 dollar. Add this item to our monthly expense list
# 5. You returned an item that you bought in a month of April and
# got a refund of 200$. Make a correction to your monthly expense list
# based on this
#### answer 1
expense = [2200,2350,2600,2130,2190]
print(expense, "initial list")

#In Feb, how many dollars you spent extra compare to January?
feb = expense[1]-expense[0]
print(feb, "was spent more in feb in comparision to january")

#Find out your total expense in first quarter (first three months) of the year.
first_quarter = expense[0]+expense[1]+expense[2]
print(first_quarter, "was the money spent in quarter 1")

# June month just finished and your expense is 1980 dollar. Add this item to our monthly expense list
expense.append(1980)
print(expense, "added month june")

#You returned an item that you bought in a month of April and got a refund of 200$. Make a correction to your monthly expense list based on this
#april month 2130, expense[3]
aprilReturn = expense[3] - 200
print(aprilReturn, "after $200 return") 
expense[3] = aprilReturn
print(expense, "updated april return")
